WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Speaker 1: Kyle Rittenhouse is doing&nbsp;
his rounds in conservative circles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.120
And the latest on him is that there's actually&nbsp;
a dispute between him and Texas A&amp;M University&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.880
over whether he's going to be going to&nbsp;
school there in the fall and taking classes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.760
Kyle said recently on the Charlie Kirk show&nbsp;
that he was going to be going to the university.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.640
The university, however, says otherwise. They&nbsp;
say that he has not been admitted and won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.680
be taking classes there. How on earth did&nbsp;
this happen? Let's first go to the clip of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.640
Kyle explaining to Charlie Kirk that&nbsp;
he is going to become an Aggie and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.520
putting on the Texas A&amp;M cap to celebrate.
Speaker 5: He's ready to make. This is like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.680
he's ready to make it. Wow, everybody. It's a&nbsp;
big deal right here on the Charlie Kirk Show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:51.040
Kyle Rittenhouse is announcing that he's an Aggie.
Speaker 6: So I'm going to be going there and it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.000
going to be awesome. Beautiful&nbsp;
campus, amazing people, amazing food.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.680
We went to Dixie to check in there. Best burgers.
Speaker 5: I've ever. That's why he's going.&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.160
Speaker 6: Texas chicken.
Speaker 5: Everybody. Now, do you know what they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:10.320
say at A&amp;M? They say gig him, gig them. And you&nbsp;
know how they say hello. They say howdy. Howdy. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.720
there you go. And so you're going to you're going&nbsp;
to be are you going to join the corps cadets?&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.960
Speaker 6: I haven't decided yet. I may.
Speaker 1: Well, that was all very interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.400
But the university disputes Kyle's claim on this.&nbsp;
Kelly Brown, who's the spokesperson for Texas A&amp;M,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.920
said, quote, He has not been admitted as a student&nbsp;
this summer or fall. Now, typically, when you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.240
one person claiming one thing and another person&nbsp;
claiming another, you have to sort of weigh the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.400
arguments to determine who's in the right and&nbsp;
who's in the wrong or maybe who's telling the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.720
truth and who's not telling the truth. With the&nbsp;
case like this, though, it's pretty clear that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.080
whatever Texas A&amp;M says goes like they're going to&nbsp;
be the correct ones in all this because it's up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.840
them. Right, that they don't want to allow him as&nbsp;
a student at the school, then he's not going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.720
going to that school. And that's just kind of the&nbsp;
end of that. Like I could say that I'm going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.040
Harvard or Yale or wherever to take classes, but&nbsp;
if those schools don't actually admit me, then I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:06.560
not going to be going to those universities. But&nbsp;
with regard to this Texas A&amp;M situation, I just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:12.480
wonder exactly how it happened. Right. Like. Was&nbsp;
he sent a denial letter, but he thought it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.680
an acceptance letter. Was he initially accepted?&nbsp;
And then they decided to rescind the acceptance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:22.240
Was there just some incredible misunderstanding?&nbsp;
What exactly happened? I mean, maybe there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:27.200
a planned charade with all this where he wanted&nbsp;
to force the university's hand into allowing him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.240
to go to the school. And maybe he wanted to make&nbsp;
some broader point to a right wing audience about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.080
liberal indoctrination and cancel culture at&nbsp;
college campuses. I'm just not exactly sure. Funny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.840
enough, Kyle has been working on a grift he calls&nbsp;
the Media Accountability Project or Team Map.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.120
I don't know why they didn't just go with MAP for&nbsp;
the acronym. They went with Team App, but team app&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.400
has the purpose of suing people for defamation&nbsp;
and going after the corporate press because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.160
Kyle felt like he was defamed during his murder&nbsp;
trial. And so he wants to get revenge against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.080
a bunch of people. But it's like one of those&nbsp;
things where, Kyle, if you're going to be doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.600
this, you're going to be working for team app.&nbsp;
You can't be going on Charlie Kirk's show and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:11.200
saying things that aren't true because maybe the&nbsp;
organization is going to have to go after you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:18.160
Before this, Kyle was taking classes at ASU,&nbsp;
Arizona State University, and he dropped the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:23.760
classes to focus on the homicide trial. He wanted&nbsp;
to resume classes there after the trial ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.680
but a bunch of students had an uproar and&nbsp;
the university decided to cut ties with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.880
You said in a follow up tweet that actually he's&nbsp;
going to be going to Blinn College, a community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:38.560
school out in Texas, tweeting, Unfortunately, the&nbsp;
end of my high school career was robbed from me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.240
I didn't have the time other students&nbsp;
get to properly prepare for the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.280
I look forward to attending Blinn College District&nbsp;
this year, a feeder school for Texas A&amp;M. I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:52.720
excited to join Texas A&amp;M in 2023, so apparently&nbsp;
he's going to blend college, although how can we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:57.520
know for sure? Because he wasn't exactly accurate&nbsp;
when it came to the Texas A&amp;M situation. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.280
maybe in a week or two we'll find out that he&nbsp;
actually wasn't admitted there. And wouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.000
that be something? And you have to wonder also&nbsp;
if this is going to cause a wave of students to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.960
leave Blinn College to transfer somewhere else&nbsp;
because they just don't want to associate with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:16.240
Kyle Rittenhouse. And I feel mixed feelings about&nbsp;
that sort of thing, because on the one hand, those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:21.760
students have every right to transfer if they just&nbsp;
don't want to associate themselves with Kyle. On&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.920
the other hand, Rittenhouse was put through the&nbsp;
criminal justice system, and he was found not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:32.960
guilty by a jury of his peers. And so there's this&nbsp;
idea that he should be allowed to rejoin society,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.120
and that can include seeking higher levels of&nbsp;
education and trying to better himself and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.280
these different things. So I do think he should&nbsp;
be able to go to college somewhere. But when when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.440
you're talking about some specific college that&nbsp;
has to let him in or doesn't have to let him in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:49.040
that's where it gets tricky because the colleges&nbsp;
have every right to make their own decisions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.360
The students who go to those schools, they have&nbsp;
every right to make those decisions. So that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.520
the latest on Kyle Rittenhouse apparently&nbsp;
becoming a college student in the fall.

